Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: tegra30: surface-rt: drop the WLAN wake interrupt

mwifiex requests the PU5 host-wake IRQ as IRQF_TRIGGER_LOW, while the line is active high
(ACPI: Level, ActiveHigh, PullDown). With the 14.62.17.p215 combo firmware needed for Bluetooth
the line idles low, so arming it in mwifiex_enable_wake() fires at once, calls pm_system_wakeup()
and every suspend fails with -EBUSY. Wake-on-WLAN is not used; drop the interrupt.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
@@ -551,8 +551,14 @@
 			compatible = "marvell,sd8897";
 			reg = <1>;
 
-			interrupt-parent = <&gpio>;
-			interrupts = <TEGRA_GPIO(U, 5) IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			/*
+			 * No wake interrupt: PU5 is the WLAN host-wake line (ACPI:
+			 * level, active high, pull-down), but mwifiex requests it as
+			 * IRQF_TRIGGER_LOW. With the 14.62.17.p215 combo firmware
+			 * (needed for Bluetooth) the line idles low, so arming it at
+			 * suspend fires at once and aborts every suspend (-EBUSY).
+			 * Wake-on-WLAN is not used; power button and lid still wake.
+			 */
 		};
 
 		// TODO test SDIO bluetooth binding
